.TH RPVIEW 1 "October 6, 2026" "MLKit @PACKAGE_VERSION@" "MLKit tools"
.SH NAME
rpview \- display MLKit region profiles and allocation-site occupancy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rpview
.RI [ profile.rp ]
.RB [ \-o " output" ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rpview
reads a binary region profile produced by an MLKit program compiled with
.B \-rp
and generates a standalone interactive HTML report, an SVG graph, or
newline-delimited JSON records.
The default input is
.B profile.rp
and the default output is
.BR profile.html .
.PP
The HTML report includes region and stack graphs, snapshot-range selection,
thread and worker filters, and allocation-site occupancy when recorded.
For a selected region with matching compiler metadata, Region slice shows
function definitions, region bindings and region instantiations.
Allocation sites provides a flat table and is the fallback when a slice
is unavailable. Static region relationships describe possible flow, not
observed call paths.
.PP
Occupancy describes objects present at a snapshot, not cumulative allocation
volume. For a range of snapshots, the allocation table uses the snapshot
with the largest selected payload and identifies it explicitly.
Finite-region storage is included in stack usage.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print usage information and exit.
.TP
.BI "\-o " file
.TQ
.BI "\-\-output " file
Write to
.IR file .
Use
.B \-
for standard output. The input file cannot also be the output file.
.TP
.BI "\-\-format " format
Select
.BR html ,
.BR svg ,
or
.BR json .
Otherwise the format is inferred from the output suffix:
.B .svg
selects SVG,
.B .json
or
.B .jsonl
selects JSON, and other suffixes select HTML.
Without an output filename, SVG goes to
.B profile.svg
and JSON goes to standard output.
JSON output contains one profile record per line.
.TP
.BI "\-\-ir\-dir " directory
Add a fallback search location for moved IR companions. May be repeated.
Normally companions are found beside the object paths recorded in the profile.
Matching build identity and integrity checks are required.
.TP
.BI "\-\-caption " text
Override the report or graph caption.
.TP
.B \-\-sites
Generate an SVG graph of object payload occupancy split by allocation site.
Requires SVG output and a recording made with
.B \-rp_region
set to a binding or
.BR all .
With all-region recordings, contributions are combined across regions.
Profiling descriptors, page headers, unused space and stack storage
are excluded.
Do not combine this option with a metric other than
.BR total .
HTML reports expose recorded site occupancy without this option.
.TP
.BI "\-\-regions " n
Show the largest
.I n
region bands (or site bands with
.BR \-\-sites ),
combining the remainder as Other. Default: 9. Use 0 for all bands.
.TP
.BI "\-\-metric " name
Choose
.B total
(the default: regions and ML stack),
.B stack
(ML stack, including finite regions),
.B pages
(region-page capacity),
.B page_footprint
(page capacity minus unused tails),
.B large_bytes
(large-object storage),
.B finite_bytes
(the legacy finite-reservation field, zero in current profiles), or
.B descriptor_bytes
(infinite-region descriptors).
.TP
.BI "\-\-scope " view
Choose
.B all
(the default),
.BI thread: n ,
.BI worker: n ,
or
.BI cpu: n .
Use \-1 for an unavailable worker or CPU identity.
The requested scope must be present in the recording.
.TP
.BI "\-\-group " name
Set the initial HTML region-table grouping to
.B aggregate
(the default),
.BR region ,
.BR thread ,
or
.BR worker .
.TP
.BR \-\-show\-base " / " \-\-hide\-base
Show or hide source base names. Default: hidden.
.TP
.BR \-\-show\-kind " / " \-\-hide\-kind
Show or hide region kinds. Default: hidden.
.TP
.BR \-\-show\-type " / " \-\-hide\-type
Show or hide region types. Default: hidden.
.TP
.BR \-\-show\-peak " / " \-\-hide\-peak
Show or hide the process-wide peak page-capacity reference line.
Default: hidden.
This is not an exact maximum of combined region and stack usage.
.TP
.BR \-\-legend\-right " / " \-\-legend\-below
Choose the initial HTML legend placement and compact naming style.
Default: right. The SVG legend always appears inside the graph on the right.
.SH RECORDING A PROFILE
Compile with
.B \-rp
and pass runtime profiling options inside
.B +RTS
and
.B \-RTS
blocks. For example:
.PP
.nf
mlkit \-rp \-o program program.mlb
\&./program +RTS \-rp \-rp_region all \-rp_interval 10ms \-RTS
rpview profile.rp \-o profile.html
.fi
.PP
For an individual binding, replace
.B all
with the unit-and-region identifier reported by rpview, such as
.BR UNIT:163 .
Runtime profiling options belong to the executable, not to rpview.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
rpview profile.rp \-o regions.svg \-\-regions 12
rpview profile.rp \-\-sites \-o sites.svg
rpview profile.rp \-\-sites \-\-scope thread:0 \-o thread.svg
rpview profile.rp \-\-format json > records.jsonl
rpview profile.rp \-\-ir\-dir /moved/build \-o report.html
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.B profile.rp
Default binary input profile. Current profiles use format version 10;
unsupported older formats must be regenerated.
.TP
.IB object .ir
Compiler-generated IR companion (normally ending in
.BR .o.ir ).
The HTML report embeds matching IR and site locations and can then be viewed
offline without the original files. Missing or mismatched companions leave
profile measurements usable, with navigation unavailable for affected sites.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success. A nonzero status indicates an invalid option,
unreadable or invalid input, or an output error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mlkit (1),
.BR reml (1)
.PP
MLKit documentation: https://elsman.com/mlkit/
